$2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 22%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Dream Finders Homes, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.1B market cap on $4.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $126M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +8.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (77.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","ca