 its 52-week range, 42% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 73% and a beta of 1.14, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.46 vs 5y 1.27), so read it loosely.","About $10.9M trades a day, enough to build a position, and interest is running hot at 2.4x its yearly average volume.","In past sell-offs it fell 64% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 67% below its blended-model fair value of $37.67, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 29%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","Multiples send mixed signals against Consumer Cyclical peers: cheaper on P/E 13.1 vs 19.3, richer on EV/EBITDA 18.8 vs 11.2 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 40% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of -11.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 18.1% (vs the 8% bar)."],"prof":["ROIC of 37% clears the cost of capital of 11.0% by 26pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.53).","It burns cash (FCF margin -3%).","Earnings quality is a concern: a weak Piotroski score of 1/9, cash conversion of only -0.46x and high accruals (+8.5% of assets).","ROE of 15% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.4x net debt to EBITDA ($234.8M of cash against $1.6B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 2.0x.","The value-trap profile is elevated (52/100); see the breakdown below."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.0% over 3 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 29%).","At current returns, reinvesting 2% of profits supports about 0.9% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (0.6% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own 20.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 96%.","Insider trading is two-way: 9 purchases and 11 sales over the past year, net $7.4M sold.","It returns 3.7% a year to shareholders (3.7% in buybacks).","Short interest is elevated at 77.5% of the float, 7.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,911 employees, each generates about $2.3M of revenue, 5.9x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 22.4% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$66K per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $5.4M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $13K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":61,"head":"Invest: trades 67% below fair value of $37.67; ROIC 37.1% vs WACC 11.0%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 47, gates 12/26)","Trades 67% below fair value of $37.67","ROIC 37.1% vs WACC 11.0%","Revenue grew 9.0%/yr over 3y","P/E 13.1x vs sector 19.3x"],"cons":["FCF margin 2.9% (burns cash)","Interest coverage only 2.0x","Piotroski F-score 1/9","EV/EBITDA 18.8x vs sector 11.2x","Heavy insider selling ($7.4M net over 12 months)"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":32.02,"vc":{"base":37.67,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":37.67,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.2941,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"DFH","date":"2026-11-06"}